WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:06.990
Existence is strange and there’s no way
we can ever manage to understand all the many

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.430
mysteries of life, the universe and everything.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:14.440
When we come across something we don’t understand,
most of us turn to teachers, parents, smart

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.630
friends and probably Wikipedia, in an attempt
to sort out what’s what.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:23.890
Some people though, like to close their eyes,
stick out their finger and believe whatever

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.730
crazy solution it lands on.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.769
And this isn’t just reserved for the darkest
corners of the internet, many well-known public

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:35.090
figures and celebrities have dived head first
into the pool of pseudoscience, conspiracies,

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.160
and good old fashioned nonsense.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:47.970
Today we look at 5 famous people with outrageous
theories and beliefs.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:53.100
Gravity seems to be a problem in a number
of wild theories but one of the best surely

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.860
has to come from internet personality David
Avacado Wolfe.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:03.890
He’s the least famous person on this list,
but he deserves first billing because of the

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.520
sheer ludicrousy of his beliefs.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.840
You probably all have a friend who shares
his steady stream of vague and generally harmless

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.640
motivational memes.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:19.110
He has almost 6 million followers on Facebook
and built a career as a raw food enthusiast,

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.070
promoting a variety of super foods and supplements.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:28.620
Oh and he beliefs gravity doesn’t exist
as we know it, it is actually a toxin that

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.960
we should get rid of.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:35.130
There are many videos of him, both interviews
and recordings of public lectures, where he

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.110
puts forward a range of theories about various
foods and the body.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:44.940
But his gravitationally questionable theory
is that he believes salt is basically the

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:51.240
gatekeeper of water and, to quote him, “the
reasons why the oceans are salty is that’s

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:55.730
what’s needed to hold the water onto the
earth, if that didn’t happen the water would

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.409
levitate right off the earth and that would
be the end of it.”

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:04.290
He doesn’t say what happens to unsalted
freshwater rivers and lakes but let’s assume

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:09.140
they’re tied down with magic rope or maybe
the fish just grip onto it really, really

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.140
tightly.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:13.270
He loves salt for its ability to keep water
retained in your muscles.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:18.590
He even recommends just having it around your
home to prevent allergies, insomnia and migraines.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:21.900
Have you even seen a peanut with a migraine?

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:22.900
No?

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:23.900
Exactly.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.710
But the Wolfe’s expertise do not end there.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:32.790
Here is a brief outline of some his other
wonderful theories;

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:38.569
“Chocolate lines up planetarily with the
sun, chocolate is an octave of sun energy.”

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:42.660
And that, children, is why you should always
eat up all your KitKats!

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.280
But seriously, “chocolate lines up with
the sun”, what does that even mean.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.510
Here’s another omniscient quote of his…

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:55.410
Mushroom spores can “levitate off the planet
because they are surrounded by a shell of

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:59.870
Ormus, which is actually trying to get to
the centre of the sun”

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:04.770
I don’t think mushroom takers intend to
get quite THAT high.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:11.849
In case you’re curious, ORMUS is an idea
created by David Hudson in 1975; they are

00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:17.680
precious metals without molecular bonds; so
all the atoms exist separately.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.680
And yes, you’re right, that is complete
nonsense.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.190
And one more of David Wolfe’s theories is
that:

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:27.590
“Deer antler is not a product.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:28.950
It's a cosmic substance.”

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:34.340
I’m not sure the deer will feel that way,
as you chop the space horns off their heads.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:36.459
He believes the horns make you younger.

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:40.910
Did I forget to mention he’s also a flat
earther too, along with a whole load of other

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:45.720
nonsense theories, but we’ll stop there,
I need to go and eat some salt before I float

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.140
away again.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:52.110
Another David now, this time ex-BBC sports
presenter David Icke.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.140
David Icke started out as a goalkeeper.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:59.690
Unfortunately, arthritis forced him to retire
at just 21 but he went on to carve out a successful

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:05.500
career as a sports presenter, eventually co-hosting
the BBC show Grandstand, the most watched

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.209
sports show in the UK.

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:13.489
Due to his arthritis, he began looking into
fringe medicine and new age philosophy, which

00:04:13.489 --> 00:04:18.660
led him to become involved with the Green
Party and also to an important meeting with

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.860
a psychic, who told him he had been sent to
heal the world.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.910
She didn’t say exactly what was wrong with
the world, some sort of stomach bug I presume.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:33.340
But nevertheless David Icke was the man to
heal it, apparently.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:38.510
He began developing an ever more elaborate
theory about why the world had got into such

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:43.990
a state of war, sickness and poverty, realising
that there must be a shadowy cabal behind

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.660
all the mischief.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:51.760
He believes that civilisation was set up by
a group of alien reptiles called the Babylonian

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:52.760
Brotherhood.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:57.740
Their bloodline continues to this day and
they control everything from the UN to the

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:03.570
media, led by the famous Illuminati, a mysterious
group of world leaders feared by tin foil

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:09.510
hat wearers and internet keyboard warriors
across the world, yes I’m looking at you.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:15.390
The reptiles came from a constellation called
Draco and were drawn to earth, not for the

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:21.470
margaritas and well organised bus routes,
but for the “monatomic gold”, which is

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:26.600
just another name for the ORMUS that we mentioned
earlier, that impossible form of metal where

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.390
none of the atoms are bonded together.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:33.540
Yes, you’re hearing me correctly, David
Icke believes the world is run by lizards,

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:37.590
with notable figures such as The Queen and
most prime ministers and presidents being

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:40.949
part of this omniscient lizard species.

00:05:40.949 --> 00:05:46.550
The reptiles are shape shifting and can take
human from, so you’d better keep your wits

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.550
about you.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:52.100
If you catch anyone looking hungrily at a
dead insect, then it’s probably best to

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:56.950
bow down to them in case they are one of your
overseeing lizard lords.

00:05:56.950 --> 00:06:01.410
Oh one more thing, he also believes he is
the son of god.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.410
I’ll just leave that out there.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.620
Do you believe in life after love?

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:12.300
Yes I do, Cher, but I’m not sure I believe
in life after relying solely on homeopathic

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.750
treatments.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:19.000
Cher is not alone in her support of homeopathy,
a whole host of stars from Pamela Anderson

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:24.960
to Tina Turner, Monica Bellucci and many others
have all come out in favour of it.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:30.190
Now, alternative medicine is a complicated
field, containing many treatments that may

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:36.320
do real good but have yet to be proven scientifically;
things like acupuncture, traditional Chinese

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:38.340
medicine and chiropractic for example.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:42.670
There is a lot of anecdotal evidence about
their effectiveness but this has not been

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:45.270
backed up by clinical testing, yet.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:50.300
The same cannot be said however about homeopathy.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:56.569
Trial after trial has proven, without a doubt,
that the practise has no benefits, beyond

00:06:56.569 --> 00:06:58.150
the placebo effect.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:03.770
In one of the most recent tests, Professor
Paul Glasziou, from Bond university in Australia,

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:12.410
oversaw 176 individual studies and found absolutely
no difference between homeopathy and the placebo

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.819
effect for 68 different illnesses.

00:07:15.819 --> 00:07:23.069
Hopefully, they can now begin looking into
other more important theories such as; “If

00:07:23.069 --> 00:07:28.420
eating carrots helps night vision, if I eat
rabbits will I see in infa-red?”

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:32.350
So, what is homeopathy?

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:39.759
Invented by Samuel Hahnemann in 1796, it follows
three laws; the law of similars, the law of

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:42.450
infinitesimals and the law of succussion.

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:46.639
If the last one sounds like a made up word,
well that’s because it is.

00:07:46.639 --> 00:07:51.599
The law of similars means finding a cure that
is similar to the symptoms, such as caffeine

00:07:51.599 --> 00:07:55.610
for insomnia or onions to treat the streaming
eyes from hay fever.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:08:01.669
Then, the law of infinitesimals means the
more you dilute the substance in water, the

00:08:01.669 --> 00:08:08.150
more it increases its potency which is just
as ludicrous and contradictory as it sounds.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:13.680
The law of succussion just tells you to shake
or tap the container during each mix, so that

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.970
the water maintains a “memory” of the
substance.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:24.330
A lot of medicines are sold as 30C or 100C,
where the C stands for centesimal.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:29.090
1C is one drop of the substance added to 99
drops of water.

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:34.769
2C is one drop taken from that the previous
solution (which remember is 1% substance,

00:08:34.769 --> 00:08:39.569
99% water) and added to another 99 drops of
water.

00:08:39.569 --> 00:08:47.480
So 30C is this same process repeated 30 times
over, making it one part per million million

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:52.660
million million million million million million
million million (1 in 1060).

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:57.579
Numbers this big are kind of meaningless so
let me give you an analogy; to dilute one

00:08:57.579 --> 00:09:03.579
full drop of a substance in a 30C solution,
you would need enough water to cover every

00:09:03.579 --> 00:09:08.420
single planet in 500 million universes.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:12.300
So I’ll get a bucket, you better start that
rain dance.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:17.470
Basically, when you buy homeopathic treatments,
you are literally paying for very expensive

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:18.470
water.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:23.850
When asked, most homeopathy consumers thought
they were actually taking pills containing

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:30.029
some kind of herbal extracts, but in reality
the original substance which was diluted in

00:09:30.029 --> 00:09:36.040
it was lost long ago during the repeated dilution
process.

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:39.819
What you’re left with, is water infused
sugar pills.

00:09:39.819 --> 00:09:45.470
But, having said all this, the placebo effect
is real, it even works on animals, and something

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:51.009
with a long standing history like homeopathy,
even if it is based on a scientific falsehood

00:09:51.009 --> 00:09:58.230
and we have repeatedly proved that it doesn’t
work, is actually still quite likely to work

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:03.839
and be effective on individuals who “believe”
it to be true, because their placebo effect

00:10:03.839 --> 00:10:06.249
after the treatment will be more powerful.

00:10:06.249 --> 00:10:12.380
Now, if homeopathy requires you to reject
some of your understandings of science, Grammy

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:18.790
nominated rapper B.o.B would like you to tear
up all your text books and make a new paper

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:21.120
mache model of the world.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:26.050
In his single Flatline he laid out his belief
that we live on a flat earth.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:31.160
He claims we have all been “Indoctrinated
in a cult called science” and calls out

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:36.809
famous astrophysicist Neil De Grasse Tyson,
claiming he has been paid off.

00:10:36.809 --> 00:10:42.610
The scientist, along with his nephew, even
created a retaliation rap.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:47.739
How did B.o.B end up with his bizarre conclusion
that the world is a spinning plate?

00:10:47.739 --> 00:10:52.290
Mankind has actually known the world is round
for a very long time since it explains the

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:57.540
way ships disappear over the horizon and why
during a lunar eclipse it is possible to see

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:03.279
the shadow that Earth makes on the moon and
you can quite clearly see that it’s a sphere.

00:11:03.279 --> 00:11:08.029
Flat Earthers believe the world is a disc
with the Arctic Circle in the middle and the

00:11:08.029 --> 00:11:11.829
Antarctic acting as a wall of ice surrounding
the big plate.

00:11:11.829 --> 00:11:17.199
You can’t walk over the edge because the
wall is guarded by NASA, possibly all disguised

00:11:17.199 --> 00:11:18.199
as penguins.

00:11:18.199 --> 00:11:21.680
Now I’m sure you have some questions like;
what about the sun?

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.139
What about planes and satellites?

00:11:23.139 --> 00:11:27.459
And “If earth is a plate, does it mean we’re
someone’s lunch?”

00:11:27.459 --> 00:11:32.490
According to flat earthers the sun and moon
are apparently spheres measuring 51 kilometres

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:38.620
across and they move in circles above the
earth, just under 5000 kilometres away, shining

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:40.439
down like spotlights.

00:11:40.439 --> 00:11:44.999
The sun has a slightly spiralled orbit to
account for its changing position in the seasons.

00:11:44.999 --> 00:11:50.189
There’s also an anti-moon, which causes
eclipses, and is made of crackers so you can

00:11:50.189 --> 00:11:54.249
eat it together with the cheese from the actual
moon.

00:11:54.249 --> 00:11:56.579
Oh wait, that’s Wallace and Gromit.

00:11:56.579 --> 00:12:01.609
How the sun stays up there is a different
matter since gravity isn’t real.

00:12:01.609 --> 00:12:08.839
According to their theory, the earth is accelerating
upwards at 9.8 m/s2, like we’re on some

00:12:08.839 --> 00:12:11.959
sort of interstellar pancake elevator.

00:12:11.959 --> 00:12:17.769
So when you slip, you’re not falling, the
world is just high fiving you in the face.

00:12:17.769 --> 00:12:21.889
All of NASAs achievements have been faked
of course and every shot of the round earth

00:12:21.889 --> 00:12:25.499
is just a nifty bit of photo-shopping.

00:12:25.499 --> 00:12:31.290
And when it comes to air travel, well all
GPS has been rigged so pilots think they are

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:36.170
travelling around a sphere but in fact are
just wasting all our time, taking the scenic

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:38.199
route in a big circle.

00:12:38.199 --> 00:12:42.550
The approach of the believers is to follow
something called the Zetetic Method which

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:46.470
values sensory observation above everything
else.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:50.759
So if the world looks flat, it must be flat,
right?

00:12:50.759 --> 00:12:55.920
By this logic, that tree is not far away,
it’s just very small and Donald Trump is

00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:01.369
exactly what he appears to be; an angry genetically
modified potato.

00:13:01.369 --> 00:13:06.480
Billy Corgan sprang to fame in the 90s as
the face of the band Smashing Pumpkins, who

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.989
became one of the largest rock bands of the
era.

00:13:08.989 --> 00:13:14.779
Their albums Mellon Collie and the Infinite
Sadness and Siamese Dream are ranked at 82

00:13:14.779 --> 00:13:21.689
and 362 in the Rolling Stone Magazine’s
list of greatest albums of all time.

00:13:21.689 --> 00:13:28.170
But Billy dreams no longer, recently describing
himself and Motley Crue drummer, Tommy Lee,

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.600
as “awake”.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:33.879
This is conspiracy theory lingo for seeing
what is really going on behind the shadowy

00:13:33.879 --> 00:13:35.019
curtain.

00:13:35.019 --> 00:13:39.569
And one of his current theories of choice
is the notorious chemtrails.

00:13:39.569 --> 00:13:43.309
When you look up into the sky, on a bright,
cloudless day, you’ll occasionally see the

00:13:43.309 --> 00:13:46.569
white plume, left in the wake of a passing
plane.

00:13:46.569 --> 00:13:51.240
Corgan, along with other stars such as Beck
and Kylie Jenner, believe that these clouds

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:56.799
are chemicals that the government is intentionally
pumping into the atmosphere.

00:13:56.799 --> 00:13:58.569
Why would they do this?

00:13:58.569 --> 00:14:03.319
Well perhaps to make people sick and get money
through pharmaceutical sales, maybe as some

00:14:03.319 --> 00:14:08.339
sort of mind control technique, weather modification,
or perhaps just to use the sky as a gigantic

00:14:08.339 --> 00:14:09.699
etch-a-sketch.

00:14:09.699 --> 00:14:12.740
In reality, these trails are caused by a couple
of factors.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:16.399
Most importantly, the exhaust coming from
the engines is hotter than the surrounding

00:14:16.399 --> 00:14:20.720
air so this difference in temperature allows
water to condense and then freeze, thanks

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:23.619
to the ambient temperature of the high altitudes.

00:14:23.619 --> 00:14:28.529
The particles in the exhaust, such as soot
and sulphur compounds, often serve as a site

00:14:28.529 --> 00:14:31.600
for this condensation and freezing to take
place.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:35.970
It’s also possible for the change in pressure,
caused by the wings and the body of the plane,

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:38.620
to act as a trigger.

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:43.959
These “contrails” (condensation trails)
can remain for minutes or hours, depending

00:14:43.959 --> 00:14:46.869
on the atmospheric conditions at the time.

00:14:46.869 --> 00:14:52.740
These trails may have an environmental impact,
since they can form sizeable clouds, but their

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:57.220
effect is limited to how they reflect heat
radiation, rather than the chemical content

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:59.290
of the clouds themselves.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:06.230
Even if Chemtrail believers reject these explanations,
there’s still a major flaw in the theory

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:11.009
since, given the height of the planes, any
chemicals being sprayed out would dissipate

00:15:11.009 --> 00:15:17.750
over hundreds of miles and lose their potency,
long before they reached the ground below.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:21.240
But as for Billy, he still believes that we
cannot be saved.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:27.529
Musicians, nutritionists and sports presenters
are one thing, but what happens when the world’s

00:15:27.529 --> 00:15:32.499
most powerful man has a bizarre theory close
to his heart?

00:15:32.499 --> 00:15:37.979
Former US president Ronald Reagan was an avid
believer in Numerology.

00:15:37.979 --> 00:15:41.910
Numerology covers a range of superstitions
about the relationship of numbers with people

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:47.749
and events, often in the realm of the paranormal
and relating to divination and astrology.

00:15:47.749 --> 00:15:52.791
Some form of number based belief is common
in many cultures, with lucky and unlucky numbers

00:15:52.791 --> 00:15:57.519
being created from the sounds and symbols
of the words, or perhaps with their religious

00:15:57.519 --> 00:16:04.269
connections, such as the Holy Trinity or the
twelve apostles in Christianity and May 4th

00:16:04.269 --> 00:16:05.540
in Jediisim.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:10.939
For Reagan, led largely by his wife Nancy
and her favourite astrologer Joan Quigley,

00:16:10.939 --> 00:16:15.509
this mostly manifested itself in how he scheduled
certain events.

00:16:15.509 --> 00:16:21.679
He delayed his inauguration as Governor of
California by 9 minutes to put it at the most

00:16:21.679 --> 00:16:23.079
opportune moment.

00:16:23.079 --> 00:16:29.200
He even used numerology to decide on the set
up of the Reykjavík Summit in 1986, where

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:33.279
Reagan and Gorbachev laid the groundwork for
the end of the cold war.

00:16:33.279 --> 00:16:37.759
I would not have liked to have been the translator
who had to tell Gorbachev “we’re just

00:16:37.759 --> 00:16:40.199
waiting untill Mars enters Uranus.”

00:16:40.199 --> 00:16:46.959
Maybe his many psychics did help him though
as he was able to finally overcome the Curse

00:16:46.959 --> 00:16:48.040
of Tippecanoe.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:52.679
9th president William Harrison was involved
in a war with a Native American tribe called

00:16:52.679 --> 00:16:56.279
the Shawnee, including the Battle of Tippecanoe.

00:16:56.279 --> 00:17:04.189
Supposedly, a Shawnee prophet called Tenskwatawa
cursed Harrison and since then every president

00:17:04.189 --> 00:17:10.549
elected on a 20th year anniversary of William
Harrison (1840) has died in office.

00:17:10.549 --> 00:17:14.050
This includes Lincoln (1860), Garfield (1880),
McKinley (1900) and JFK (1960) as well as

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:19.110
Harding’s (1920) heart attack and Roosevelt’s
(1940) cerebral haemorrhaging.

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:25.089
But after Reagan became president the curse
seems to have been broken.

00:17:25.089 --> 00:17:30.909
Thanks to Reagan’s belief in magic numbers,
George W Bush, elected in 2000, was able to

00:17:30.909 --> 00:17:36.769
survive 3 attempted assignations, an attack
by a journalist’s shoe, choking on a pretzel

00:17:36.769 --> 00:17:41.509
and was one of the lucky members of the White
house not to be shot in the face by Dick Cheney

00:17:41.509 --> 00:17:42.710
while hunting.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:48.090
It’s somehow reassuring to know that no
matter how famous or powerful you become,

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:53.049
you can still be scared of monsters under
the bed and believe in the magical cures and

00:17:53.049 --> 00:17:55.730
treatments that could fix us all in an instant.

00:17:55.730 --> 00:18:01.049
I personally, sometimes have the creepy feeling
that I’m being watched by mysterious strangers

00:18:01.049 --> 00:18:25.190
from around the world.

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:30.750
Ha, silly isn’t it?

